//
// Phase C4: every baseline_768 shape resolves through kernel_registry.
//
// The sub-phase's whole point is that `registry_lookup.gemm_config()` stops
// raising for the 36 projection GEMMs the case matrix's baseline_768 family
// needs. This is the regression test for that, and it is deliberately the cheap
// half: it re-reads the rows the sweep wrote and resolves each one. It does not
// re-measure anything. The sweep that produced the rows takes an hour on real
// hardware and is `make registry-sweep`, not a lit test.
//
// npu2 in the filename is the TARGET THE ROWS DESCRIBE -- kernel_registry is an
// NPU2-only registry (`"target": "npu2"` in the JSON) and every tile config in
// it was measured on AIE2P. The check itself dispatches nothing and needs
// neither a device nor Peano, which is exactly why it is cheap enough to gate
// on. Adding a hardware requirement here would only stop the regression from
// surfacing on a compile-only runner.
//
// The count is part of the gate. A registry write that dropped half the family
// would still let the surviving shapes resolve, and a check that only looked for
// a final PASS would report success on it -- so the number of resolutions is
// pinned, and nothing may resolve after the last one.
//
// So is the METHOD. `gemm_builder.gemm_method_spec` knows only `fused-cast` and
// `drain`; a row whose high-precision winner was recorded as `direct` would
// resolve here perfectly happily and then raise `unknown gemm method` inside
// every model that read it. Requiring one of the two buildable names turns that
// into a failure here instead of a failure three phases downstream.
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for its directives, so naming
// one in prose -- even inside a comment -- registers as a second directive and
// leaves the test UNRESOLVED. Describe them, never spell them out.
//
// RUN: python3 %S/registry_sweep.py --family baseline_768 --verify-resolution | FileCheck %s
//
// CHECK-COUNT-36: [resolve] {{[0-9]+x[0-9]+x[0-9]+}} ({{.*}}) -> {{fused-cast|drain}} {{[0-9]+/[0-9]+/[0-9]+/[0-9]+}}
// CHECK-NOT: [resolve]
// CHECK: PASS: all 36 baseline_768 shapes resolve
